If I have the choice between the two I like to carry them as
alternate wields.  Most monsters keep Magicbane.  The bigger
fights use "x" to switch to the heavier damage Stormbringer.
When a mean spellcaster is the opponent keep Magicbane and
use as many methods as possible to take it out quickly.  I
tend to run wizards this way.

> As far as thrown daggers go, they are damn heavy.... on the other
> hand, 300 arrows are pretty heavy too.

Daggers are high damage per throw and never disappear - Early
game advantage.  Arrows are high damage per weight and nearly
stop disappearing once blessed and with maxed out luck - Late
game advantage.  Being able to carry so many more arrows
means higher total damage so eventually in a game arrows start
being a better option than daggers.

For a class able to become expert in both like samurai I'll rush for
expert in dagger in the early game then use a bow often enough
to reach expert by the Castle and use arrows for much of the late
game.  But Samurai doesn't get the complexity of chosing among
Magicbane, Stormbringer or the Longbow.  For Samurai the
choice of Snickersnee or Excalibur is much simplere.

For a ranger carrying Magicbane this means using "x" to alternate
between it and the Longbow.  Goodbye Stormbringer as an instant
switch during heavy combat.

Weight is an eternal issue for all characters.  How many missiles
of what type is a constant tradeoff.  What type of armor and how
many pieces, what other items to carry, all of the choices effect
how many missiles to carry before getting Burdened.


